# Priyosha Charity Organization — Caddy reverse proxy (EXAMPLE)
#
# This file fronts the Next.js frontend (port 3000) and the Go api-gateway
# (port 8080) with automatic HTTPS. It is an example to copy to your server,
# not a live deploy.
#
# Live domain: priyoshacharity.com
#   Primary site: https://priyoshacharity.com  ->  localhost:3000
#   API:          https://api.priyoshacharity.com  ->  localhost:8080
#   www.priyoshacharity.com redirects to https://priyoshacharity.com
#
# 1. In your DNS provider, create A records pointing at your server's IP:
#      priyoshacharity.com      ->  <server IP>
#      www.priyoshacharity.com  ->  <server IP>
#      api.priyoshacharity.com  ->  <server IP>
# 2. On the server, set DOMAIN in .env to your domain:
#      DOMAIN=priyoshacharity.com
#    Caddy reads it from the environment as {$DOMAIN}.
# 3. Run Caddy with this file, e.g. `caddy run --config deploy/Caddyfile`
#    or via the caddy Docker image. Caddy obtains and renews Let's Encrypt
#    certificates automatically — no manual certificate step.
# 4. Keep ports 80/443 open to the internet; keep 3000/8080 reachable only
#    from localhost / the proxy.
#
# {$DOMAIN} expands from the DOMAIN environment variable (Caddy 2 syntax).
# If you prefer Nginx, the equivalent is: server_name priyoshacharity.com;
# proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:3000 for the site and http://127.0.0.1:8080
# for /api, plus a www -> bare-domain redirect.

{$DOMAIN} {
	reverse_proxy localhost:3000
}

www.{$DOMAIN} {
	redir https://{$DOMAIN}{uri} permanent
}

api.{$DOMAIN} {
	reverse_proxy localhost:8080
}
